{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"that person logan","id":"519566652824616973","is_bot":0,"username":"thatpersonlogan"},"author_id":"519566652824616973","channel_id":"736446567862632508","content":"Wren walks back to her room. She lays on her bunk, her hand off the side of the bed, fingers grazing the floor. She flips onto her stomach and looks under her bed. A little ways under the bed, is a hole.","created_at":"2020-07-25T19:58:21.796000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"736673720889770044","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"that person logan","id":"519566652824616973","is_bot":0,"username":"thatpersonlogan"},"author_id":"519566652824616973","channel_id":"736446567862632508","content":"Wren takes a piece of paper out of her journal and begins to craft a note: \n“||To: Skitter\nI wish you didn’t have to stay in the shadows on board. I wish we could just sit together and talk about our treehouses and play with the hermit crabs. That would be fun. But we only have one week left until we get to Roanoke. Are you excited? I am. I’m mostly excited to see the stars and the fireflies. I’ve heard there are fireflies everywhere. \n\nEnclosed in this letter you will also find \n-A loaf of my mother’s Berry Bread\n-3 pieces of paper \n-3 colored pencils\n\nWant to hang out later? \nWarm Regards,\nWren Rosewood||”\n<@!692746345387130900>","created_at":"2020-07-25T20:06:13.502000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-25T20:06:28.556000Z","id":"736675699368263770","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
